  "namedChanges": [
    "the imports are replaced by imports of the peers: `./config` by `vault-origin-rule`; `./token`, `./bearer` and `./dpop` by `lws-session-bridge` (with `import * as dpopModule` for the module the app read as a namespace); `./records` by `lws-records` 0.2.0; `./vaultSets` and `./recordPlane` by `lws-vault-sets`; `./recordTypes` by `record-types`; `./stakeholderKinds` (`GILBVEDA_MASTER_ORIGIN`) by `term-origin`; `./termSearch` by `ontology-reads`; the type `RecordRelation` by `relation-role`; `typeCurieFromJsonLd` by `type-curie`; `parseGrantPrincipals` and `DirectShareEntry` by `direct-shares`; `shareRefusalMessage` by `share-refusal`; the type `FolderPart` by `folder-part`; the names the taken code does not use are dropped from the import lists",
    "`BASE_ORIGIN` is `baseOrigin()` at `relationWrite.ts:115`, `relationWrite.ts:305`, `entityShare.ts:103` and `entityShare.ts:625`",
    "`GILBVEDA_MASTER_ORIGIN.replace(...)` (`relationWrite.ts:187`) is `termOrigin().replace(...)`",
    "the constant `PUBLIC_GRANTEE` (`publicAccess.ts:18`) is the function `publicGrantee()`, built from `termOrigin()`, and its seven uses (`publicAccess.ts:27`, `entityShare.ts:553` and `:561`, `folderPublic.ts:195`, `:196`, `:239`, `:240` and `:310`) call it",
    "the method of the request is passed at the three bearer fallbacks of write requests: `relationWrite.ts:326` is `bearerHeaderFor(url, \"PUT\")`, `relationWrite.ts:509` is `bearerHeaderFor(url, \"POST\")`, `entityShare.ts:584` is `bearerHeaderFor(url, \"POST\")`; the other site, `relations.ts:87`, is a GET and keeps the default",
    "comments that name a host are reworded, `BASE_ORIGIN` in a comment reads `baseOrigin()`, and person and agent names in comments are generic; no code changed"
